WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:34.960
[Music]

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:37.410
[Narrator:] This is Hillendale, USA.

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:40.760
Just one American town.

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:43.660
Of course, it looks like a lot of other American
towns.

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:45.320
Your town.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:53.460
And like your town, it has its businesses,
its homes, its cars, and its people, and children.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:57.760
Children just like youngsters in your town
and dentists like Doc Jenkins.

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:02.760
[Music]

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:06.180
[Dr. Jenkins:] How are you, Ms. Carter?

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:08.160
[Joe:] Hi, doc. How you doing?

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:10.400
[Dr. Jenkins:] Hello, Joe. Pretty well, thank you.

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:11.640
[Jimmy:] Hi, Dr. Jenkins.

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:12.860
[Dr. Jenkins:] Hiya, Jimmy.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:19.040
[Narrator:] But there is something different
about this town, something vitally different.

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:23.560
A vital difference that at present affects
mainly the children,

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:27.360
and will affect them as long as they live.

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:35.240
You can't see the difference in their clothes
or in the way they walk or play.

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:41.020
You may not even notice it in their smiles,
and yet that is where the difference is,

00:01:41.210 --> 00:01:42.320
in their smiles,

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:44.740
in their mouths.

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:48.280
Inside their mouths.

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:53.700
You may not see, but the trained eyes of Miss
Jones, the dental hygienist can see...

00:01:53.701 --> 00:01:58.979
can see that something has happened to the
teeth of the young children.

00:01:58.979 --> 00:02:02.469
Something that today is almost a dental miracle.

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:11.200
For today, Miss Jones finds only one cavity
for every three she found seven years ago.

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:14.620
[Music]

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:17.650
Seven years ago something happened in this
town.

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:19.770
Something very simple happened.

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:23.310
Seven years ago something was added to this
water.

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:28.870
Added to this town's drinking water.

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:37.280
It did something to the teeth or for them,
and the children's teeth

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:41.010
just don't have as many cavities anymore.

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:42.900
And here's how it happened.

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:48.940
[Dr. Jenkins:] Here's something interesting
Miss [?],

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:51.239
about fluoride in drinking water.

00:02:51.239 --> 00:02:52.750
Listen to this.

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:58.299
A considerable amount of scientific evidence
shows that children born and reared in areas

00:02:58.299 --> 00:03:03.300
having fluoride in their drinking water have
fewer cavities than have children

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:05.639
using fluoride-free water.

00:03:05.639 --> 00:03:10.660
This scientific evidence meant simply that
this chemical would save teeth.

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:16.080
Now, Doc Jenkins is in the business of saving
teeth, and he knew what a job it is to

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:20.030
cope with all the cavities in children's teeth.

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:26.050
Doc knew that dental decay is the most widespread
of all diseases.

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:29.959
That there are literally millions of neglected
tooth cavities.

00:03:29.959 --> 00:03:33.880
He knew that the average man or woman can
look forward, without pleasure,

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:38.890
to losing half their teeth before reaching
40.

00:03:38.890 --> 00:03:43.810
He knew that tooth decay begins early in life, in childhood, and that the time to start doing something

00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:48.889
about it is early, when children are less than eight years old, six, four,

00:03:48.889 --> 00:03:51.449
two years, even earlier.

00:03:51.449 --> 00:03:54.699
Before tooth decay has a chance to affect
their health.

00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:00.960
And while he knew, of course, that youngsters themselves could do some things,

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:05.820
he recognized that he and the other grownups of his town would have to do a great deal more.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:12.360
The Doc got all the information he could about the then-new idea of fluoridation to save teeth.

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:19.290
The facts were exciting, and Doc determined to do something about it.

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:23.740
At dental conventions, he began bending the ears of his fellow dentists.

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:31.199
Soon, full of enthusiasm, he got, at a most
propitious moment, the ear of the mayor.

00:04:31.199 --> 00:04:33.810
[Mayor:] Fluoridation, eh?

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:37.680
And so the mayor asked interested civic-minded
groups to meet with the town council

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:41.940
to hear the opinion of experts: dentists, physicians,

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:46.259
the dental director of the state health department,
and local health department people.

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:51.880
[Mayor:] Now I'm going to ask Mr. Evans, chairman
of the fluoridation committee,

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:54.000
to take over the meeting.

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:55.100
Mr. Evans.

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:58.260
[Mr. Evans:] Thank you, mayor.

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:02.300
First of all, I'd like to call on Dr. Foster.

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:09.100
[Dr. Foster:] Well, speaking for myself as
well as other dentists in this area,

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:10.780
we are for fluoridation.

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:15.580
We dentists are in business to save teeth,
not just to fill them.

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:17.750
[Mr. Evans:] Thank you, Dr. Foster.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:19.760
And now we're going to hear from Dr. Harris

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:22.100
of our local health department.

00:05:22.101 --> 00:05:26.099
[Dr. Harris:] Our health department has received
some studies on fluoridation

00:05:26.099 --> 00:05:27.740
from the state health department.

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:32.100
[Narrator:] The local health department learned that children who drink water containing one part

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:37.760
of naturally-occurring fluoride per million
parts of water have two-thirds less tooth decay.

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:42.620
Two-thirds less decay than children drinking
ordinary water.

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:47.400
[Dr. Harris:] That's why we at your health
department feel that fluoridation

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:50.620
merits your approval.

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:52.540
[Man in bowtie:] I'd like to say something.

00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:55.580
I've heard that fluoride will make your teeth
look ugly.

00:05:55.980 --> 00:06:00.240
Now, we don't want our children's teeth to
look bad with black and yellow stains.

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:02.100
Let's give up the idea.

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:04.000
[Man with mustache:] He's right.

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:05.740
And it makes the bones brittle, too.

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:07.980
Does all sorts of things to your health.

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:11.060
[Chairman:] Let's hear what our state dental
director has to say about this matter.

00:06:11.069 --> 00:06:13.860
[State Dental Director:] Those statements
are not right.

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:18.169
Facts in our possession indicate that there
is absolutely no danger.

00:06:18.169 --> 00:06:23.199
[Narrator:] The state dental director's office
had proof that only excessive amounts of fluoride

00:06:23.199 --> 00:06:28.050
can cause mottling of teeth, and that hundreds of thousands of people have used natural fluoride

00:06:28.050 --> 00:06:31.129
in the right amounts all their lives without
harmful effects.

00:06:31.129 --> 00:06:35.310
[State Dental Director:] I'm sure the physician
on this committee will agree that these people

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:36.819
are just as healthy

00:06:36.820 --> 00:06:39.439
as people who drink ordinary water.

00:06:41.320 --> 00:06:43.320
[Physician:] That's exactly right.

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:51.140
A great deal of sound medical evidence suggests that these chemical compounds will not harm

00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:56.400
the human system in any way when used in the recommended proportions, and further,

00:06:57.220 --> 00:07:06.660
will save teeth, and therefore make it easier for us doctors to preserve the health of the people of Hillendale.

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:10.879
[Older woman in glasses and hat:] I like this
fluoridation idea.

00:07:10.879 --> 00:07:15.840
[Narrator:] At meetings of women's groups,
PTAs, and so on, the idea of better teeth

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:16.840
for children,

00:07:16.840 --> 00:07:18.960
with less strain on the pocketbook, had a
strong appeal.

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:24.920
[Water department supervisor:] Well, we people in the water department are ready to do the job.

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:29.700
[Man in back wearing glasses:] Have you got
the facts in regards to the cost of this?

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:32.780
[Mr. Evans:] Yes, sir, we have gone into the
matter quite fully.

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:37.020
[Narrator:] The low cost of installation and
maintenance was fully explained,

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:41.500
and then recommendations were presented to
the people of Hillendale.

00:07:42.780 --> 00:07:48.240
Community-wide discussion started, and a hot
discussion it was on both sides of the question.

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:52.440
[Man outdoors wearing hat:] What do you mean,
fluoride?

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:56.300
I like my water clean and pure, not doped
up with a lot of chemicals.

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:00.660
[Man on the street smoking cigar:] Anything
that will give my kids good teeth

00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:03.360
and save me dough, boy, I'm for that.

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:06.440
[Gas station worker:] Fluoridation.

00:08:06.440 --> 00:08:07.440
Stupid.

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:10.520
[Shirtless man working outside:] Well, I tell
you this.

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:12.160
If it's going to help the kids, it's a very
good.

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:15.020
Me, I oughta know. I got eight.

00:08:16.840 --> 00:08:18.180
[Narrator:] Yes, sir.

00:08:18.189 --> 00:08:20.199
When town meeting time rolled around again,

00:08:20.199 --> 00:08:21.849
the folks in Hillendale were pretty excited.

00:08:21.849 --> 00:08:24.400
[Man wearing tie and glasses:] I'd like to
ask a question.

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:25.479
Won't the water taste funny?

00:08:25.479 --> 00:08:29.240
[Water department supervisor:] Fluoride will
add neither taste nor odor to the water.

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:32.930
[Woman wearing pearls:] What will it do to
my clothes when I wash them?

00:08:32.930 --> 00:08:36.200
[Water department supervisor:] Madam, fluoride
will not color the water

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:39.260
nor will it harden it or soften it.

00:08:39.270 --> 00:08:42.120
[Man wearing polka-dot tie:] Well, now, tell
me this.

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:44.640
How's it going to affect my liver?

00:08:44.640 --> 00:08:47.160
[Audience laughs.]

00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:50.580
[Physician:] Medically speaking, it will have
no effect.

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:53.540
[Jim:] Some towns, they put fluoride in the
water.

00:08:53.540 --> 00:08:55.260
Others, they take it out.

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:56.260
How come?

00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:58.680
[Mr. Evans:] Well, Jim, let me explain that.

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:04.900
Towns that have too much natural fluoride
in the water must take it out,

00:09:04.900 --> 00:09:09.270
but towns that have no fluoride, they must
add enough to do the job.

00:09:09.270 --> 00:09:11.690
[Jim:] But why add the stuff?

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:15.160
I like my water the way it is, not medicated.

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:18.430
Fluoridation is just another name for mass
medication.

00:09:18.430 --> 00:09:22.720
[Physician:] Why, you don't add fluoride to
cure a disease.

00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:26.280
You add fluoride to prevent disease, tooth
decay.

00:09:26.280 --> 00:09:31.780
Why, we've been adding chlorine to our water
for a long time now to prevent disease.

00:09:31.780 --> 00:09:33.160
No one calls that mass medication.

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:37.520
[Woman with young daughter:] Will it hurt
our goldfish or guppies?

00:09:37.520 --> 00:09:39.860
[Audience laughs]

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:42.880
[Physician:] The amount we propose will harm
no living creature.

00:09:44.340 --> 00:09:48.040
[Man holding baby:] What I want to know is,
how much is it going to cost me?

00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:51.080
[Mayor:] It'll cost you about ten cents a
year per person.

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:52.740
That's just a drop in the bucket.

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:58.880
Because the fact is, every one of you citizens of Hillendale can pay your share of thirty years

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:03.560
of fluoridation for the price of filling one
tooth.

00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:08.540
[Narrator:] And that was about it, for the
people of Hillendale had the courage of their convictions.

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:13.200
Decided to pioneer on the strength of the
available evidence,

00:10:13.210 --> 00:10:14.210
even before fluoridation was endorsed,

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:18.030
as it is today, not only by the United States
Public Health Service,

00:10:18.030 --> 00:10:22.580
but also by the American Dental Association,
the American Public Health Association,

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:27.390
and other national health organizations.

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:31.320
After the town council acted, well, everybody
sort of waited.

00:10:31.320 --> 00:10:36.680
Went about their business as usual, but the
day the equipment was installed at the waterworks,

00:10:36.680 --> 00:10:41.790
now that was the day.

00:10:41.790 --> 00:10:43.660
Some wanted to see the feeder.

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:47.830
Some wanted to see what the fluoride looked like, how it was weighed and put into the water.

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:54.220
And the feeder pump that was designed to add
just one part of fluoride

00:10:54.220 --> 00:10:58.220
to each million parts of water.

00:10:58.220 --> 00:11:05.650
It was a big day for Doc Jenkins and all those
who had fought to put over the idea.

00:11:05.650 --> 00:11:08.140
Some wanted to see the fluoride in the water.

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:17.410
But of course, they couldn't see it, or smell
it, and they couldn't taste it.

00:11:17.410 --> 00:11:22.300
They couldn't see or taste the fluoride then,
any more than the youngsters can see or taste it

00:11:22.340 --> 00:11:26.840
back here in the schoolhouse today, where
they've been drinking this fluoridated water

00:11:26.840 --> 00:11:28.910
for seven years.

00:11:33.020 --> 00:11:37.520
But as a matter of fact, you can see the fluoride
now, where Doc sees it,

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:39.950
in the dental records of the town.

00:11:39.950 --> 00:11:45.650
For the records show that already, two out
of every three cavities have been prevented

00:11:45.650 --> 00:11:46.650
in the teeth

00:11:46.650 --> 00:11:50.910
of the little people of Hillendale.

00:11:50.910 --> 00:11:54.350
[Music]

00:11:54.350 --> 00:12:00.600
And you can see it in the smiles of these
children and all the children that come after them.

00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:08.300
The happy, shining smiles of their own healthy teeth.

00:12:08.300 --> 00:12:13.080
[Music]

00:12:13.180 --> 00:12:19.400
[The End]

00:12:19.560 --> 00:12:30.420
[This film was made with the cooperation of
the people of Newark, Delaware]

